      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: require exact claims for direct cloud cleanup",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- require canonical lease IDs before DigitalOcean, Linode, Vultr, or Scaleway resources enter Crabbox inventory\n- require exact provider/account-or-project/resource-bound local claims before reuse, stop, or cleanup\n- keep claimless canonical resources read-only until explicit `--reclaim` adoption; never synthesize destructive ownership from remote tags\n- preserve interrupted-create recovery while validating the exact stored provider identity, and prevent read-only resolve paths from writing claims\n- document the ownership boundary in provider and stop documentation\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/811\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go test -race ./...`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `scripts/test-go-modules.sh`\n- `scripts/check-go-coverage.sh 90.0` (90.0%)\n- `node --test scripts/*.test.js` (362 passed)\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- Worker format, lint, both typechecks, 760 tests, and all dry-run builds\n- deadcode and CLI build\n- focused race tests for exact provider claims, canonical-ID alias denial, provider-scope conflicts, and read-only status resolution\n- three autoreview passes; clean after fixing provider-scope and canonical-ID fallback findings\n\n## Exact-head live proof\n\nCandidate: `7d58d5c6d53e7a71247faa7c9b872d6ae05af57b`\n\n- DigitalOcean: authenticated from empty inventory; provisioned a real Droplet and managed SSH key; reached ready; ran `echo ok` over SSH; listed the exact claimed resource; stopped it; verified final Crabbox inventory `[]` and no managed-key residue.\n- Linode: authenticated from empty inventory; provisioned a real instance; reached ready; ran `echo ok` over SSH; listed the exact claimed resource; stopped it; verified final Crabbox inventory `[]` and no local-key residue.\n- Scaleway: authenticated from empty inventory; provisioned a real project/zone-bound instance and managed SSH key; reached ready; ran `echo ok` over SSH; listed the exact claimed resource; stopped it; verified final Crabbox inventory `[]` and no managed-key residue.\n- Vultr: pending because an authenticated API credential is not yet available. Keep this PR unmerged until the same exact-head create/use/stop/empty-inventory proof passes for Vultr, or that provider-specific gate is explicitly waived.\n",
        "branch": "codex/issue811-provider-ownership",
